<meta type=article title="Meta allowlist elements fixture" author="Test Author" doi="10.5555/test.2024" license="CC BY 4.0" lang="en-US" version="1.0.0" keywords="elephants, conservation, climate">
</meta>

<section | The lifted meta kwargs now render as real elements>

This fixture exercises the five `<meta>` allowlist members that previously
rendered as `<span data-acadamark-unknown="…">` for want of vocabulary
entries: `doi`, `license`, `lang`, `version`, `keywords`. The kwargs lift
to child tags at the normalize-to-canonical gate (per the apparatus-tag
reconciliation), and now that the vocabulary entries exist, they render
as real Layer 1 elements: `<doi>`, `<license>`, `<lang>`, `<version>`,
`<keywords>`.

<abstract |
A short abstract for the document, included to confirm `<abstract>` —
which was already in the vocabulary, contrary to the backlog claim —
continues to render correctly.
>
